// RELATED: crates/ethereum/payload/src/lib.rs (block payload builder)
// reth's block proposer (EthereumPayloadBuilder) builds execution payloads including blob transactions.
// Blob transactions have already been validated in the mempool via validate_blob() which calls
// into the c_kzg library. Field element range checks are delegated to the external c_kzg library.
// The payload builder pulls pre-validated txs from the pool; it does not re-validate KZG proofs.
//
// NOTE: In reth's architecture, the execution layer (reth) handles blob tx validation via c_kzg.
// The block proposer is the consensus layer client (beacon node), which is a separate component.
// Reth provides execution payloads via Engine API; the beacon node assembles the final block.
// Field element range validation (bytes_to_bls_field) for EIP-7594 cells is a beacon-layer concern.
